# Scratch workspace for local sub-agent / DAG testing (see ui-webui chat workspace picker).
/tmp/
.omo/*
.ruff_cache/

# Sub-agents are opt-in, one folder at a time: a folder here can hold a docker
# image tar or a private checkout, so the default stays "ignored" and each
# tracked one is named. Everything unsafe *inside* a tracked folder - secrets,
# rendered configs, run/session/cache/ledger state, the vendored .venv - is
# covered by that folder's own .gitignore, which git only consults once the
# parent stops being excluded.
subagents/*
!subagents/raven-code/
!subagents/raven-oncall/
!subagents/raven-research/

# Report assets AGENTS.md bars from the repo whatever carries them. The
# vendored upstream trees ship benchmark PDFs, doc diagrams and a demo
# screenshot; two of them are over the 1 MiB limit that CI enforces, and the
# exemption for application source trees does not reach in here.
#
# Kept in step with BLOCKED_ASSET_EXTENSIONS in scripts/check_large_files.py,
# which is the list CI actually enforces -- a narrower list here would let the
# next upstream refresh track a file that then fails CI a long way from its
# cause. These trees are web-adjacent, so an icon or a webp is a plausible
# thing for the next release to carry.
subagents/**/*.aac
subagents/**/*.apng
subagents/**/*.avi
subagents/**/*.avif
subagents/**/*.bmp
subagents/**/*.flac
subagents/**/*.flv
subagents/**/*.gif
subagents/**/*.heic
subagents/**/*.heif
subagents/**/*.htm
subagents/**/*.html
subagents/**/*.ico
subagents/**/*.jfif
subagents/**/*.jpeg
subagents/**/*.jpg
subagents/**/*.m4a
subagents/**/*.m4v
subagents/**/*.mkv
subagents/**/*.mov
subagents/**/*.mp3
subagents/**/*.mp4
subagents/**/*.mpeg
subagents/**/*.mpg
subagents/**/*.oga
subagents/**/*.ogg
subagents/**/*.ogv
subagents/**/*.opus
subagents/**/*.pdf
subagents/**/*.png
subagents/**/*.svg
subagents/**/*.tif
subagents/**/*.tiff
subagents/**/*.wasm
subagents/**/*.wav
subagents/**/*.webm
subagents/**/*.webmanifest
subagents/**/*.webp
subagents/**/*.wmv

